@codelaw/rules-ts

The rules are reimplementations written for codelaw. Their `ported_from:`
fields name the typescript-eslint rules (https://typescript-eslint.io, MIT
License) whose documented behaviour they reproduce; no typescript-eslint code
or documentation text is included.

The rules whose `ported_from:` names a `biome/` rule reproduce the documented
behaviour of Biome 2.6.4 (https://biomejs.dev, MIT License); no Biome code or
documentation text is included.

The rules ported from typescript-eslint's stylistic and strict sets in W-139
follow the same terms: behaviour only, written fresh (typescript-eslint, MIT License).

`ts/no-mergeable-namespace` reproduces the documented behaviour of TSLint's
rule of that name (https://palantir.github.io/tslint, Apache License 2.0); no
TSLint code or documentation text is included.
